</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">At the start of Stage 2, we use the converged checkpoints and generate <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> rollouts per question.
Then, we discard samples where all rollouts are correct (i.e., overly easy examples) to improve efficiency.
This filtering is performed after Stage 1, since the trained checkpoints are stronger than the initial models.
The detailed stage 2 configurations are given in <a href="#A2.T4" title="In Appendix B Implementation Details ‣ Nudging the Boundaries of LLM Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
